  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate resilience and adaptation facility for technologies: improving rural adaptive capacity and resilient livelihoods in the Southern, Western and Central provinces of Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate resilience and adaptation facility for technologies (CRAFT) : improving rural adaptive capacity and resilient livelihoods in the Southern, Western and Central provinces of Zambia project is a strategic initiative developed by UNIDO and the Government of Zambia for submission to the Adaptation Fund. It aims to strengthen smallholder adaptive capacity and build resilient rural livelihoods in Zambia#s Southern, Western, and Central Provinces. CRAFT focuses on developing a functioning local market for climate adaptation technologies, products, and services by linking smallholder demand with MSME supply, strengthening community financial resilience, and improving district-level planning through updated Integrated Development Plans (IDPs). Grounded in locally led adaptation (LLA) principles, CRAFT complements Zambia#s National Adaptation Plan (NAP) and Eighth National Development Plan (8NDP) by mobilizing private-sector innovation and community participation to deliver scalable, context-specific resilience solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
